course: dictionary
lesson: 7436
title: Pollute and our planet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To pollute means to make air, water or land dirty and harmful by adding waste, smoke or chemicals. Pollute is a verb, so it changes its ending: pollutes, polluted, polluting. «Smoke from vehicles, factories and burning rubbish pollutes the air.»
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. Smoke, vehicles, factories and rubbish are the things that do the polluting. The word pollutes tells you what they do to the air: they make it dirty and harmful to breathe.
explain: Often we hear it in the passive, like «The river is polluted.» This means something has been made dirty and harmful by people or things, such as waste or chemicals. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The river is made dirty and harmful" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Pollute means to make air, water or land dirty and harmful.
fact: «Burning fossil fuels pollutes the air and adds carbon dioxide, which warms the Earth's climate.»
fact: We can reduce pollution by recycling, walking and cycling.
fact: «Wild axolotls... are critically endangered because of drained, polluted water and introduced fish.»
fact: «Polluted» means made dirty and harmful, so «pick berries away from roads» keeps them safe from traffic fumes.
exercise: «Smoke from vehicles, factories and burning rubbish pollutes the air.» What does pollutes mean here? | Makes the air cool and fresh | *Makes the air dirty and harmful | Lets the sunshine through | Fills the sky with clouds
exercise: «Burning fossil fuels pollutes the air and adds carbon dioxide.» Which word tells what fossil fuels do to the air? | *pollutes | air | fossil | carbon
exercise: Which is a good way to reduce pollution? | Dropping litter on the path | Leaving the tap running | *Walking or cycling instead of driving | Burning more rubbish
test: «The lake is polluted.» What does polluted mean? | Made into a park | Made deep and wide | *Made dirty and harmful | Made cold and frozen
test: Why are wild axolotls critically endangered? | They are too big to swim | Too many people eat berries | *Drained, polluted water and introduced fish | Their tails are dark brown
exam: Why should you wash berries before eating them, and pick them away from roads? Because roadside berries may be polluted by what? | Snow | *Traffic fumes | Rain | Sunshine
